# Build-context exclusions for docker/Dockerfile.
#
# Builds use the REPO ROOT as context (`docker/build.sh` runs
# `docker buildx build -f docker/Dockerfile .`; CI uses `context: .` and
# `file: docker/Dockerfile`). Docker reads `<context>/.dockerignore` or, with
# BuildKit, `<Dockerfile path>.dockerignore`. This file is the second form, so
# every pattern below is relative to the repo root, not to docker/.
#
# The Dockerfile COPYs only: s1-secops-mcp/package.json, s1-secops-mcp/index.js,
# s1-secops-mcp/lib/, s1-secops-mcp/tools/, s1-secops-mcp/scripts/, CLAUDE.md
# and docker/entrypoint.sh. Nothing below may match those paths.

.git
.github
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
**/.venv
**/.pytest_cache

# s1-secops-mcp ships from local source, so what sits beside it in the build
# context matters. s1-secops-mcp/data/ is git-ignored and holds only local
# exports; no code references it and the Dockerfile COPYs path by path and
# never names it. Excluding it here as well keeps local files out of the
# context and out of any layer.
s1-secops-mcp/data/
data/

# Build artefacts
s1-secops-skills-plugin/dist/
s1-secops-mcp/dist/
s1-secops-mcp/mcpb/
*.tar.gz
*.zip
*.skill
*.plugin
*.mcpb

# Heavy reference / test data not needed inside the image
mgmt-console-api/spec/
**/tests/
tests/
spec/
docs/
assets/

# Editor & OS junk
.vscode/
.idea/
**/.DS_Store
**/*.swp
**/*.log

# Office docs (sometimes dropped in the repo root for one-offs)
*.pptx
*.docx
*.xlsx
*.pdf

# Windsurf workflow files (not needed at runtime)
.windsurf/
